[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2726920495","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2726920495","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103901","id":2726920495,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iiYEv","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-15T18:32:49Z","updated_at":"2025-03-15T18:32:49Z","body":"While this looks like a valid bug, you could easily avoid it by connecting `pressed` signal and setting `action_mode` to Button Press.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2726920495/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2726926230","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2726926230","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103901","id":2726926230,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iiZeW","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-15T18:40:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-15T18:41:22Z","body":"I see one problem here. When the button gets disabled, the pressed state is reset silently. Which means that `button_down` signal has no equivalent `button_up`.\r\n\r\nI think it would make sense to emit `button_up` if the button was pressed while being disabled, and it should be documented.\r\n#81532 did something similar.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2726926230/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727017427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2727017427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103901","id":2727017427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iivvT","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-15T21:56:34Z","updated_at":"2025-03-15T21:59:55Z","body":"> While this looks like a valid bug, you could easily avoid it by connecting `pressed` signal and setting `action_mode` to Button Press.\r\n\r\nYes, but as I said, it is a design choice to use `button_down` instead of `pressed`. Game designers much better than me swear on down instead of press: https://x.com/id_aa_carmack/status/1787850053912064005\r\n\r\nCurrently the only way to get around the bug would be to delete the button immeadiately on `button_down`, then create a new identical button to the same position than the original and set the new button disabled. When the new button is enabled, the first down click would work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727017427/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727019461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2727019461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103901","id":2727019461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iiwPF","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-15T22:02:03Z","updated_at":"2025-03-15T22:02:03Z","body":"> it is a design choice to use button_down instead of pressed\r\n\r\nPressed can be either \"down\" or \"up\", it's up only by default.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727019461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727032277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2727032277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103901","id":2727032277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iizXV","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-15T22:28:47Z","updated_at":"2025-03-15T22:28:47Z","body":"> Pressed can be either \"down\" or \"up\", it's up only by default.\r\n\r\nThat's right, it took me a while to find the setting. If a `Button`'s `Action Mode` is changed to `Button Press` instead of the default `Button Release`, `pressed` signal starts to work like a `button_down` signal, but without this bug.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727032277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831953865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2831953865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103901","id":2831953865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ozC_J","user":{"login":"7hells","id":111233836,"node_id":"U_kgDOBqFLLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111233836?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells","html_url":"https://github.com/7hells","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/7hells/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-26T08:16:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-26T08:16:00Z","body":"> > Pressed can be either \"down\" or \"up\", it's up only by default.\r\n> \r\n> That's right, it took me a while to find the setting. If a `Button`'s `Action Mode` is changed to `Button Press` instead of the default `Button Release`, `pressed` signal starts to work like a `button_down` signal, but without this bug.\r\n\r\nI have encountered this problem.  For me, the `button_down` and `pressed` signals are equally important because I need `button_down` to detect dragging and `pressed` to detect confirmation.  The worst part is that I happen to need to temporarily `disable` the button to avoid interacting with other buttons when it is pressed.  Just as you said, I have tried methods such as transmitting signals and forging mouse input, but none of them can solve this problem.  I hope this bug can be fixed.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831953865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831987853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103901#issuecomment-2831987853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos